#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations.rst:17
msgid ""
"ROS can use different middleware vendors to support communication between "
"nodes, depending on your platform, requirements, and distribution. This "
"article introduces RMW implementations, identifies the default vendor, and "
"links to guidance for DDS and non-DDS middleware options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations.rst:28
msgid ""
"By default, ROS 2 uses DDS as its `middleware <https://design.ros2.org/"
"articles/ros_on_dds.html>`__. It is compatible with multiple DDS or RTPS "
"(the DDS wire protocol) vendors. There is currently support for eProsima's "
"Fast DDS, RTI's Connext DDS, Eclipse Cyclone DDS, and GurumNetworks GurumDDS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations.rst:32
msgid "It also supports non DDS RMW implementations such as Zenoh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations.rst:34
msgid ""
"See `REP-2000 <https://reps.openrobotics.org/rep-2000/>`__ for supported RMW "
"vendors by distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RMW-Implementations.rst:36
msgid "The default RMW vendor is eProsima's Fast DDS."
msgstr ""

